.TH SCRATCH-LINK 1 "2026-11-24" "scratch-link-gtk" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
scratch-link \- local WebSocket bridge between Scratch and Bluetooth peripherals
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scratch-link
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B scratch-link
runs a small local WebSocket server that implements the Scratch Link network
protocol.  Scratch connects to it on
\fBws://127.0.0.1:20111/scratch/ble\fR for Bluetooth LE extensions and on
\fBws://127.0.0.1:20111/scratch/bt\fR for Bluetooth Classic (RFCOMM)
extensions.
.PP
Bluetooth access goes through BlueZ on the system D-Bus bus; no extra
capabilities, NSS database changes or hosts-file entries are required.
.PP
When a display server is available the program opens a status window with
the adapter state, recently discovered devices and a log.  Without a display,
or when \fB\-\-headless\fR is given, it runs without a user interface and is
suitable for a systemd user service.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-port=\fIPORT\fR
Listen on \fIPORT\fR instead of 20111.
.TP
.B \-\-listen\-address=\fIADDRESS\fR
Bind to \fIADDRESS\fR instead of 127.0.0.1.  The default keeps the service
reachable only from the local machine; binding to 0.0.0.0 or :: lets any host
that can reach the port control connected Bluetooth devices.
.TP
.B \-\-adapter=\fINAME\fR
Use the BlueZ adapter named \fINAME\fR (for example hci0).  The name is
matched against both the adapter Name and Alias properties.
.TP
.B \-\-min\-rssi=\fIDBM\fR
Do not report peripherals weaker than \fIDBM\fR (default \-90).
.TP
.B \-\-headless
Do not create a graphical interface.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose, \-v
Enable verbose protocol and Bluetooth logging.
.TP
.B \-\-version, \-V
Print the program version and protocol version, then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-h
Show the command line summary and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/scratch-link/settings.ini
Per-user settings written by the preferences dialog.  Command line options
take precedence over this file for the current run.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DISPLAY, WAYLAND_DISPLAY
When neither is set, the program falls back to headless mode.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run the graphical application:
.PP
.RS 4
scratch-link
.RE
.PP
Run as a background service on a non-default adapter:
.PP
.RS 4
scratch-link \-\-headless \-\-adapter=hci1
.RE
.PP
Inspect protocol traffic while connecting a micro:bit:
.PP
.RS 4
scratch-link \-v
.RE
.SH NOTES
Scratch's micro:bit extension requires the Scratch-specific micro:bit
firmware.  Factory or MakeCode firmware exposes different GATT services and
will connect but fail to subscribe; the verbose log reports the missing
0xf005 service.
.PP
The service listens on the loopback interface by default.  Exposing it on a
non-loopback address is only safe on a trusted network.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR bluetoothctl (1)
.PP
Project home page: https://github.com/yetist/scratch-link-gtk
